      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start. can u make it slightly more personalized? maybe add a line about how much we enjoyed the technical deep dive he did. also, sometimes these rejections feel a bit cold. is there a way to make it feel a bit more human without being unprofessional? like, maybe a metaphor for how hard the decision was? something about how even when things don't align perfectly it doesn't mean there wasn't a great connection?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course—here’s a revised version with a warmer, more human touch while keeping it professional:\n\n---\n\n**Subject:** Update on Senior Developer Position  \n\nDear Marcus,  \n\nThank you again for the time and energy you invested in our interview process for the Senior Developer role in Austin. We especially enjoyed your technical deep dive on cloud architecture—your ability to break down complex systems with such clarity left a real impression on our team.  \n\nAfter careful consideration, we’ve decided to move forward with another candidate whose background aligns more closely with our specific fintech needs. This was a difficult choice, and it reminded us that sometimes two things can be truly great—but not perfectly aligned, like two well-tuned instruments that don’t quite share the same key.  \n\nWe hope you know this isn’t a reflection of your strengths, which are considerable. We’re grateful for the connection we made during this process and would genuinely welcome the chance to cross paths again in the future.  \n\nWishing you all the best in your next chapter.  \n\nWarm regards,  \n[Your Name]  \n\n---\n\nThis keeps the closure clear, adds a personal touch about the deep dive, and uses a gentle metaphor to soften the finality without undermining it",
      "source": "target",
